WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.119 --> 00:00:01.761
- I surrender.

00:00:01.761 --> 00:00:03.237
- (clapping) Yeah.

00:00:03.237 --> 00:00:05.308
- You guys, (beep) this
test, this is horrible.

00:00:05.308 --> 00:00:10.308
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.678 --> 00:00:17.715
- We have a 16 year old who is
taking 'em very soon, right?

00:00:17.715 --> 00:00:20.061
- Yeah, she's super stressed out about it.

00:00:20.061 --> 00:00:22.301
- My son has taken a PSAT so far.

00:00:22.301 --> 00:00:24.612
- My son just took it, and
P.S. it was really hard.

00:00:24.612 --> 00:00:26.941
- When in doubt, you choose C right?

00:00:28.624 --> 00:00:29.372
- We read a passage, and

00:00:29.372 --> 00:00:30.917
we have to answer questions about it.

00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:33.611
- My emotions are complicated,
not readily verifiable.

00:00:33.611 --> 00:00:35.875
Like who's emotions
are readily verifiable?

00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:37.573
- I'm already zoning out.

00:00:37.573 --> 00:00:38.973
- And what I do is both a challenge

00:00:38.973 --> 00:00:40.748
to my egotism and a surrender to it.

00:00:40.748 --> 00:00:42.160
(exhaling)

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:42.877
- Deep (bleep).

00:00:42.877 --> 00:00:44.347
- It's very teenangsty.

00:00:44.347 --> 00:00:46.941
- And a lot of needlessly large words.

00:00:46.941 --> 00:00:49.622
- I don't even want to read
it, that's why I'm skimming.

00:00:49.622 --> 00:00:51.447
- Okay, which choice
provides the best evidence,

00:00:51.447 --> 00:00:53.501
for the answer to the previous question?

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:55.451
- Oh my gosh, really?

00:00:55.451 --> 00:00:56.869
- I have to go back and reread it?

00:00:56.869 --> 00:00:58.215
It was painful enough the first time.

00:00:58.215 --> 00:00:59.383
- I don't know, I don't even want

00:00:59.383 --> 00:01:00.636
to think about that question anymore.

00:01:00.636 --> 00:01:01.819
Moving on.

00:01:01.819 --> 00:01:02.724
- [blonde hair] Oh my God.
- [brunette] Oh.

00:01:02.724 --> 00:01:06.624
- That passage was obtuse,
to use an SAT word.

00:01:06.624 --> 00:01:08.321
- Two wrong, eight right.

00:01:08.321 --> 00:01:10.515
- I only have four correct, it's very sad.

00:01:10.515 --> 00:01:12.511
- (laughing) I didn't even
fill out the form properly

00:01:12.511 --> 00:01:13.904
because I'm missing one.

00:01:15.024 --> 00:01:17.684
- This is writing and language test.

00:01:17.684 --> 00:01:19.402
- Grammar Nerd Heaven.

00:01:19.402 --> 00:01:21.785
- People be oppressed and including the

00:01:21.785 --> 00:01:23.296
- Now, that's bad.

00:01:23.296 --> 00:01:24.051
- Included

00:01:24.051 --> 00:01:26.083
- So, Sarah wants to add more words,

00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:27.673
and I want to delete the whole thing.

00:01:27.673 --> 00:01:29.487
- I took me a minute to
understand actually what they were

00:01:29.487 --> 00:01:30.765
asking the question.
- [Dark Hair] Yeah,

00:01:30.765 --> 00:01:31.500
what are they asking?

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.285
I don't understand.

00:01:32.285 --> 00:01:34.744
- As an adult, I've learned
that if you don't use

00:01:34.744 --> 00:01:37.452
proper grammar, it makes
you look really stupid.

00:01:37.452 --> 00:01:39.924
- We both got seven out of nine,
we got the exact same ones.

00:01:39.924 --> 00:01:41.504
- A couple of them were tricky.

00:01:41.504 --> 00:01:43.558
- Four wrong, I'm never
gonna live this down.

00:01:43.558 --> 00:01:45.718
- I got three wrong, so six right.

00:01:45.718 --> 00:01:48.561
- When you get in that
testing environment,

00:01:48.561 --> 00:01:50.268
you start to second guess.

00:01:52.347 --> 00:01:53.885
- Math test, no calculator.

00:01:53.885 --> 00:01:54.837
- I'm sweating.

00:01:54.837 --> 00:01:57.350
- I'm having anxiety,
just like looking at this.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.652
- I feel like I have to
say, math is important kids,

00:02:00.652 --> 00:02:02.854
but it's really not.

00:02:02.854 --> 00:02:04.267
- Which of the following expressions is

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.459
equal to zero for sum value of x?

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.821
- I don't even know what
the question is asking me.

00:02:08.821 --> 00:02:11.527
- Like the names of people
I went to kindergarten with,

00:02:11.527 --> 00:02:15.624
I can recall, no problem,
but what expression is equal

00:02:15.624 --> 00:02:17.349
to zero, for sum value of x?

00:02:17.349 --> 00:02:19.027
- What's the point of the

00:02:19.027 --> 00:02:21.558
- What ever happens, it becomes
positive no matter what.

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:23.914
- Literally, nothing you
just said made sense to me.

00:02:23.914 --> 00:02:26.573
- Oh my God, I don't want to
subject my children to this.

00:02:26.573 --> 00:02:30.404
- 10 divided by zero would be, 10, right.

00:02:30.404 --> 00:02:31.276
- No, I don't think so.

00:02:31.276 --> 00:02:33.145
- No, I got it wrong 'cause
if I had gotten it right,

00:02:33.145 --> 00:02:34.769
the answer would be one half,

00:02:34.769 --> 00:02:36.001
but that's not a choice.

00:02:36.001 --> 00:02:37.456
- Do we have to divide the whole thing?

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:38.971
Like do we
- [Blonde] What, no.

00:02:38.971 --> 00:02:40.610
My brain, I cant.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:41.922
- No.

00:02:41.922 --> 00:02:43.036
- Five, out of six.

00:02:43.036 --> 00:02:44.267
- Two, out of six.

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:47.553
- I got two legitimate answers right,

00:02:47.553 --> 00:02:50.078
then I got two right by guessing,

00:02:50.078 --> 00:02:51.717
for a total of four.

00:02:53.453 --> 00:02:55.687
- I'm trying to think of like a time after

00:02:55.687 --> 00:02:57.674
you get through college,
when you really have to sit

00:02:57.674 --> 00:03:01.267
and be so focused, for so long.

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:03.264
- It's horrible, it's so hard.

00:03:03.264 --> 00:03:07.130
I'm an adult now, math,
and I don't use this,

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:08.893
in my life, math.

00:03:08.893 --> 00:03:11.041
- I still don't like testing period

00:03:11.041 --> 00:03:12.697
- Never make me do that again.

